questions.explanation:
For an ideal op-amp, the input current into the inverting terminal is zero. Due to negative feedback, \[V_{-}=V_{+}=0\] Thus, the inverting terminal is at virtual ground. Hence, the source sees only the input resistor of \(1\,\text{k}\Omega\). \[I_{i}=\frac{V_{i}}{1\,\text{k}\Omega}\] Therefore, the input resistance is \[R_{in}=\frac{V_{i}}{I_{i}}
=\frac{V_{i}}{V_{i}/1\,\text{k}\Omega}
=1\,\text{k}\Omega\] \[\boxed{\text{(c) }1\,\text{k}\Omega}\]

